( bounda_baseline_correction time_start time_end (manual 6.19), F5 T5 U9.
  The prescribed acceleration a(t) = 1 on [0,1] gets the parabola
  p(tau) = c0 + c1*tau + c2*tau^2, tau = (t - 0)/(1 - 0), fitted by least
  squares of the velocities of the time steps: p = -1, the velocity stays 0
  up to t = 1; after time_end the acceleration is not corrected, so
  v(2) = 0.1*(0.9+0.8+...+0) = 0.45. The velocity record of node 2 is not
  an acceleration and is not corrected.
  The Professional 02-08-2026 writes the same parameters (-1 0 0) but adds
  them to the bounda_time points: DIVERGENCES BASELINE-CORRECTION-SIGNAL. )
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 1
materi_acceleration
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
end_initia
inertia_apply -yes
node 1  0
node 2  1
element 1  -truss 1 2
group_type 0  -truss
group_truss_area 0  1.0
group_truss_elasti_young 0  1.0
group_truss_density 0  2.0
bounda_dof  10  1 -accx
bounda_time 10  0. 1.  0.5 1.  1. 1.  2. 0.
bounda_dof  11  2 -velx
bounda_time 11  0. 1.  2. 1.
bounda_baseline_correction 0. 1.
control_timestep 10  0.1 2.
target_item  0  -bounda_baseline_correction_parameters 10 0
target_value 0  -1. 1.e-10
target_item  1  -bounda_baseline_correction_parameters 10 1
target_value 1  0. 1.e-10
target_item  2  -bounda_baseline_correction_parameters 10 2
target_value 2  0. 1.e-10
target_item  3  -node_dof 1 -velx
target_value 3  0.45 1.e-10
target_item  4  -node_dof 2 -velx
target_value 4  1. 1.e-10
end_data
